{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01VmpDXp6tSPMYsA3kqchRXF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants me to generate worst-tier predictions for all experiments in the experiment_plan. Let me carefully go through each experiment and produce detailed predictions under the worst-case scenario defined in Phase 1.\n\nKey worst-tier definitions:\n- CLIP-ViT RSA ≈ DINO (0.35-0.42) or CLIP-ViT RSA > SigLIP (>0.60)\n- LIBERO-Spatial ordering reversal or training invariance broken\n- Reviewer consensus: scope too narrow + metric dependency unresolved\n\n\n- Core framing needs restructuring\n\nNow I'm reviewing the experiment status across the plan—most are already completed with concrete results, but plan_005 remains orphaned and needs attention for the worst-case analysis.\n\nLooking at what's left to do, I need to focus on the two planned experiments (plan_010 and plan_012) and reinterpret the finished work under worst-tier assumptions. The prompt is asking specifically for detailed data on each planned experiment, so I should identify which ones actually have that status and work from there.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":335,"cache_read_input_tokens":37581,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":335},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f38db59a-3a00-4c34-a2f2-7814e0d4d5d6","uuid":"89f97d4d-d73b-40fa-99cd-89a918bf16bb"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01VmpDXp6tSPMYsA3kqchRXF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```yaml\ntier: worst\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  CLIP-ViT 打破 VL-pretraining 解释（RSA ≈ DINO 或 RSA > SigLIP），核心 framing 需重构。\n  放弃 \"vision encoder dominance\" 作为 general claim。\n  重构方向 A: \"Fine-Tuning Teaches Routing, Not Representation\"，聚焦 Claim 2+3，Claim 1 降级为 observation。\n  重构方向 B: \"Metric Dissociation\" framing，若 CLIP-ViT RSA > SigLIP 且 R² < SigLIP，\n  则 geometric-functional dissociation 本身成为核心贡献。\n  Claim 3 的 routing-not-creating 在任何场景下都成立，是 worst case 的保底叙事锚点。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  - name: \"SigLIP+Projector RSA vs Full VLA vs DINO\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_001\"\n    description: \"SigLIP+Projector RSA 对比 Full VLA 和 DINO，证明 action-relevant 结构源自 frozen vision encoder\"\n    expected_results:\n      siglip_projector_rsa: 0.615\n      trained_with_inst_rsa: 0.501\n      untrained_with_inst_rsa: 0.485\n      dino_rsa: 0.388\n    result_rationale: >\n      此实验已完成，数据不变。但在 worst 档下，这些结果的解释力被 plan_012 CLIP-ViT 结果削弱：\n      如果 CLIP-ViT RSA ≈ 0.39（≈ DINO），则 SigLIP 的高 RSA 不来自 \"VL pretraining\" 大类，\n      而来自 SigLIP 特定训练配方（sigmoid loss + batch design）。\n      SigLIP 0.615 的优势变成一个 architecture-specific observation 而非 generalizable claim。\n      如果 CLIP-ViT RSA > 0.60（> SigLIP），则 RSA 与下游性能脱钩（OpenVLA 用 SigLIP 而非 CLIP，\n      说明高 RSA 不等于好的 VLA backbone），RSA 作为核心 metric 的 validity 被质疑。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"RSA Comparison (unchanged, but reinterpreted)\"\n        rows:\n          - { model: \"SigLIP+Projector\", rsa: 0.615, worst_interpretation: \"SigLIP-specific, not VL-general\" }\n          - { model: \"VLA trained\", rsa: 0.501, worst_interpretation: \"LLM degradation holds regardless\" }\n          - { model: \"VLA untrained\", rsa: 0.485, worst_interpretation: \"Architecture-driven, training-invariant\" }\n          - { model: \"DINO\", rsa: 0.388, worst_interpretation: \"Vision-only baseline, may ≈ CLIP-ViT\" }\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Bar chart: SigLIP >> VLA >> DINO 仍成立，但新增 CLIP-ViT bar 后 narrative 需修改\"\n    analysis: >\n      数据本身不受影响。Worst 档的冲击来自 plan_012：CLIP-ViT 的位置决定 SigLIP 优势的归因。\n      Claim 1 必须从 \"VL pretraining produces geometric alignment\" 降级为\n      \"SigLIP provides highest geometric alignment in OpenVLA\"——一个 observation 而非 mechanism claim。\n\n  - name: \"DINO baseline RSA\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_002\"\n    description: \"Standalone vision model 参照基线\"\n    expected_results:\n      dino_rsa: 0.388\n      dino_action_R2: 0.712\n    result_rationale: >\n      已完成，数据不变。Worst 档下的关键重解读：DINO RSA=0.388 可能与 CLIP-ViT 接近（worst 预测\n      CLIP-ViT RSA ∈ [0.35, 0.42]）。这意味着 CLIP（VL-pretrained）和 DINO（self-supervised）\n      在 geometric alignment 上无显著差异，VL pretraining 不是 geometric alignment 的充分条件。\n      但 DINO 的 action R²=0.712 ≈ Projector 0.706 已说明 action information presence 与\n      geometric alignment 是不同维度——这个 dissociation 在 worst 档下反而更突出。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Scatter: RSA vs R² 二维图中，DINO 和 CLIP-ViT 聚集在低 RSA / 高 R² 区域，SigLIP 独占高 RSA / 高 R² 角\"\n    analysis: >\n      DINO 数据不变，但其角色从 \"vision-only 下界\" 变为 \"与 CLIP-ViT 共同构成 non-SigLIP cluster\"，\n      强化 metric dissociation narrative。\n\n  - name: \"Per-layer RSA degradation curve\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_003\"\n    description: \"追踪 RSA 从 projector output 到 LLM 各层的衰减轨迹\"\n    expected_results:\n      proj_rsa: 0.615\n      peak_llm_rsa: 0.488\n      proj_to_l1_drop_pct: \"20-40%\"\n      total_degradation: 0.13\n    result_rationale: >\n      已完成，数据不变。Worst 档下，per-layer curve 的解释力不受 CLIP-ViT 结果影响：\n      无论 SigLIP 的 geometric advantage 来自何处，LLM 对 geometric alignment 的降解是确定的\n      （0.615→0.488）。这条证据直接支持 Claim 2（LLM redistributes），与 Claim 1 的 scope 缩减无关。\n      在重构方向 A 下，per-layer curve 升级为核心 figure（从 supporting 变为 main evidence）。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Per-layer RSA worst-tier role\"\n        rows:\n          - { metric: \"Proj→L1 drop\", value: \"0.13-0.25\", role: \"Core evidence for Claim 2, unaffected by worst\" }\n          - { metric: \"Non-monotonic pattern\", value: \"yes\", role: \"Supports redistribution narrative\" }\n          - { metric: \"All LLM >> DINO\", value: \"yes\", role: \"Architecture matters even if VL-pretraining doesn't explain SigLIP\" }\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Per-layer RSA curve: 从 Claim 1 的 supporting figure 升级为 Claim 2 的 main figure\"\n    analysis: >\n      Worst 档下此实验的价值反而上升——当 Claim 1 被降级时，Claim 2 的 LLM degradation + redistribution\n      成为论文核心贡献之一，per-layer curve 是其关键可视化证据。\n\n  - name: \"Output head analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_004\"\n    description: \"确认 SigLIP+projector frozen，LLM 权重变化不传导到表征\"\n    expected_results:\n      vision_projector_cos_sim: 1.0\n      llm_rel_change_range: [1.22, 1.37]\n      head_vs_llm_ratio: 1.12\n    result_rationale: >\n      已完成，数据不变。Worst 档下，\"SigLIP+projector frozen\" 的意义发生微妙变化：\n      原 narrative 是 \"frozen vision encoder 提供 action structure，所以 Claim 1 成立\"。\n      Worst 档下变为 \"frozen SigLIP 提供最高 geometric alignment，但这可能是 SigLIP-specific\n      而非 VL-pretraining-general\"。Frozen 属性本身仍解释 trained ≈ untrained（Claim 3），\n      所以此实验对 routing-not-creating narrative 的支持不变。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      此实验在 worst 档下对 Claim 3 的支持力不变。对 Claim 1 的支持从 \"frozen encoder is the source\"\n      变为 \"frozen encoder explains training invariance\"，scope 缩窄但逻辑链不断。\n\n  - name: \"6 probing methods × 2 benchmarks\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_005\"\n    description: \"系统性验证 trained ≈ untrained\"\n    expected_results:\n      trained_vs_untrained_delta: \"≈0 across all methods\"\n      all_methods_consistent: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      Orphaned 但子实验已完成。数据支持 trained ≈ untrained。Worst 档下此结论不受威胁——\n      training invariance 是 Claim 3 的基础，与 CLIP-ViT 结果无关。即使 CLIP-ViT 打破 Claim 1，\n      routing-not-creating 的证据链（trained ≈ untrained in distributed representations,\n      trained >> untrained in readout concentration）完全独立。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      Worst case 的保底叙事锚点。6 methods consistency 在任何档位下都是 strong evidence。\n\n  - name: \"Instruction ablation\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_006\"\n    description: \"去掉 instruction text 测 RSA 变化\"\n    expected_results:\n      delta_with_vs_no_inst: 0.004\n      gate_judgment: \"FAIL — instruction 无影响\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      已完成，数据不变。Worst 档下 instruction invariance 仍成立且价值不变：\n      它直接支持 Claim 3 的 \"三重不变性\"（training + instruction presence + instruction content），\n      与 vision encoder identity 无关。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      Instruction ablation 在所有三档下结论一致，是 Claim 3 最稳健的子证据之一。\n\n  - name: \"2×2 matrix (training × instruction)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_007\"\n    description: \"四条件全收敛验证\"\n    expected_results:\n      four_cell_range: [0.480, 0.490]\n      bootstrap_ci_includes_0: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      已完成，数据不变。2×2 矩阵在 worst 档下仍是 Claim 3 的核心证据：\n      四个 cell 收敛在 0.48-0.49 band 内，bootstrap CI 包含 0。\n      这个结果不依赖 CLIP-ViT 的位置，因为它测量的是 VLA 内部 training/instruction 的效应，\n      而非跨 encoder 的比较。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"2×2 Matrix (unchanged)\"\n        rows:\n          - { condition: \"trained+inst\", rsa: 0.488, worst_role: \"Claim 3 core\" }\n          - { condition: \"trained-no_inst\", rsa: 0.489, worst_role: \"Claim 3 core\" }\n          - { condition: \"untrained+inst\", rsa: 0.485, worst_role: \"Claim 3 core\" }\n          - { condition: \"untrained-no_inst\", rsa: 0.480, worst_role: \"Claim 3 core\" }\n    figures_description:\n      - \"2×2 heatmap: 在 worst 档下从 supplementary 升级为 main text figure\"\n    analysis: >\n      Worst 档下，当 Claim 1 降级后，Claim 3 的 2×2 matrix 成为论文最 clean 的实验设计，\n      升级为 main figure 之一。\n\n  - name: \"Random instruction control\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_008\"\n    description: \"用随机/无意义 instruction 替代真实 instruction，验证 instruction content 不影响 RSA\"\n    expected_results:\n      normal_rsa: 0.489\n      random_rsa: 0.484\n      shuffled_rsa: 0.483\n      empty_rsa: 0.472\n      max_absolute_delta: 0.017\n    result_rationale: >\n      已完成，数据不变。四种 instruction 条件下 RSA 差异 < 0.02，完成三重不变性的第三重。\n      Worst 档下价值不变——instruction content invariance 是独立于 encoder identity 的发现。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      与 plan_006、plan_007 共同构成 Claim 3 不可撼动的证据基础。Worst 档不影响。\n\n  - name: \"CKA verification\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_009\"\n    description: \"用 CKA 指标重复 RSA 发现，确认或否认 metric dependency\"\n    expected_results:\n      cka_ordering: \"untrained > trained > projector > DINO (反转 RSA ordering)\"\n      cka_last_preaction: 0.127\n      rsa_cka_dissociation: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      已完成。RSA-CKA dissociation 在 worst 档下的角色发生质变：\n      原本是 \"需要讨论的 limitation\"（metric dependency），worst 档下变成核心贡献之一。\n      如果选择重构方向 B（Metric Dissociation framing），CKA-RSA-R² 三重分离\n      本身就是方法论贡献：RSA 捕捉 geometric alignment（SigLIP wins），CKA 捕捉 global structure\n      preservation（untrained wins），R² 捕捉 functional decodability（DINO ≈ SigLIP）。\n      三个 metric 三种排序 = 单一 metric 不足以评估 VLA 表征质量。\n      CLIP-ViT 如果 RSA > SigLIP 且 R² < SigLIP，则是第四个分离维度，进一步强化此论点。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Triple Metric Dissociation (worst-tier core contribution)\"\n        rows:\n          - { metric: \"RSA (geometric)\", ordering: \"SigLIP > trained > untrained > DINO\", captures: \"local distance structure alignment\" }\n          - { metric: \"CKA (global)\", ordering: \"untrained > trained > SigLIP > DINO\", captures: \"global structure preservation\" }\n          - { metric: \"R² (functional)\", ordering: \"readout > DINO ≈ SigLIP > LLM_img_mean\", captures: \"action decodability\" }\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Triple ordering reversal diagram: 三个 metric 的排序箭头交叉，每个 metric 讲不同故事\"\n    analysis: >\n      Worst 档下 plan_009 从 P2 实验升级为核心贡献。Metric dissociation 在 best/mid 档是\n      limitation discussion，在 worst 档是 main finding。方向 B 的论文标题可能变为\n      \"No Single Metric Captures VLA Representation Quality: A Multi-Metric Dissociation Analysis\"。\n\n  - name: \"LIBERO-Spatial cross-benchmark\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_010\"\n    description: \"第三个 benchmark 交叉验证所有 claims\"\n    expected_results:\n      libero_spatial_siglip_rsa: 0.42\n      libero_spatial_trained_rsa: 0.38\n      libero_spatial_untrained_rsa: 0.40\n      libero_spatial_dino_rsa: 0.35\n      libero_spatial_training_delta_p: 0.02\n      libero_spatial_readout_delta: 0.010\n      ordering_reversal: true\n      training_invariance_broken: \"possibly — p=0.02 < 0.05\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Worst 档核心预测：LIBERO-Spatial 的 action 空间结构与 LIBERO-Goal 不同（spatial reasoning\n      vs goal-directed manipulation），可能导致：\n      (1) SigLIP RSA 从 0.615 跌至 ~0.42——SigLIP 的 geometric alignment 在 spatial tasks\n      上远不如 goal tasks 突出，因为 SigLIP 的 VL pretraining 偏向 object-centric 而非 spatial。\n      (2) 排序反转：untrained RSA (0.40) > trained RSA (0.38)——random LLM 保留更多\n      spatial structure（因为 trained LLM 的 attention 被 LIBERO-Goal 的 fine-tuning 分布偏置，\n      对 out-of-distribution 的 spatial tasks 反而更差）。\n      (3) Training invariance 边缘打破：Δ=0.02, p≈0.02——CI 不包含 0 但效应小，\n      说明 training invariance 是 distribution-dependent 而非 architectural guarantee。\n      (4) Readout concentration delta 缩小到 0.010（vs LIBERO-Goal 的 0.045），\n      因为 routing 是 task-specific learned behavior，out-of-distribution 时效果衰减。\n      综合：LIBERO-Spatial 不支持 clean Claim 3 narrative，需要加 distribution-dependency caveat。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"LIBERO-Spatial vs LIBERO-Goal Comparison (worst-tier)\"\n        rows:\n          - { metric: \"SigLIP RSA\", libero_goal: 0.615, libero_spatial: 0.42, delta: -0.195, interpretation: \"Spatial tasks expose SigLIP weakness\" }\n          - { metric: \"Trained RSA\", libero_goal: 0.501, libero_spatial: 0.38, delta: -0.121, interpretation: \"Overall alignment drops\" }\n          - { metric: \"Untrained RSA\", libero_goal: 0.485, libero_spatial: 0.40, delta: -0.085, interpretation: \"Less degradation → ordering reversal\" }\n          - { metric: \"Training Δ p-value\", libero_goal: 0.20, libero_spatial: 0.02, delta: \"n/a\", interpretation: \"Invariance breaks at p<0.05\" }\n          - { metric: \"Readout Δ\", libero_goal: 0.045, libero_spatial: 0.010, delta: -0.035, interpretation: \"Routing is distribution-specific\" }\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Side-by-side per-layer curves: LIBERO-Goal (clean separation) vs LIBERO-Spatial (messy, overlapping bands)\"\n      - \"Bootstrap CI comparison: LIBERO-Goal CI includes 0, LIBERO-Spatial CI excludes 0\"\n    analysis: >\n      LIBERO-Spatial 在 worst 档下对 Claim 3 造成最严重威胁。Training invariance 的 p<0.05 break\n      意味着 \"routing-not-creating\" 不是 universal statement，而是 in-distribution observation。\n      论文需要加 distribution-dependency qualification：\"Training teaches distribution-specific routing;\n      distributed representations remain approximately invariant within the fine-tuning distribution.\"\n      这削弱了 Claim 3 的 generality 但不 falsify 它。\n      但如果 readout Δ 也缩小到 noise level（0.010, p>0.05），则 routing narrative 本身\n      受质疑——trained LLM 在 OOD 时既不 route 也不 create，只是 pass through。\n\n  - name: \"Functional action probe (three-way)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_011\"\n    description: \"Projector / LLM / DINO 三方 functional probe 对比\"\n    expected_results:\n      projector_R2: 0.706\n      llm_image_mean_R2: 0.683\n      llm_readout_R2: 0.731\n      dino_R2: 0.712\n      untrained_readout_R2: 0.686\n      bootstrap_proj_vs_llm_p: 0.001\n    result_rationale: >\n      Orphaned 但子实验已完成，数据不变。Worst 档下 functional probe 的关键重解读：\n      DINO R²=0.712 ≈ Projector R²=0.706 (p=0.22) 已经是 worst-direction 的证据——\n      action information presence 不区分 VL-pretrained 和 self-supervised encoder。\n      如果 CLIP-ViT R² 也 ≈ 0.70（与 DINO/SigLIP 同水平），则 \"所有 modern vision encoders\n      都包含足够的 action-relevant information\" 成为 finding，而非 SigLIP dominance。\n      如果 CLIP-ViT R² < 0.65（显著低于 DINO/SigLIP），则与 CLIP-ViT RSA > 0.60 形成\n      RSA-R² dissociation（高 geometric alignment 低 functional capacity），\n      是方向 B metric dissociation 的核心证据。\n      Readout concentration（trained 0.731 >> untrained 0.686, p<0.0001）不受 worst 档影响，\n      仍是 Claim 2+3 的最强 functional evidence。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Functional Probe under Worst Tier\"\n        rows:\n          - { model: \"SigLIP+Proj\", R2: 0.706, worst_role: \"≈ DINO, not special in R²\" }\n          - { model: \"DINO\", R2: 0.712, worst_role: \"≈ Proj, action info is generic\" }\n          - { model: \"LLM img_mean\", R2: 0.683, worst_role: \"Degradation confirmed, Claim 2 holds\" }\n          - { model: \"Trained readout\", R2: 0.731, worst_role: \"Routing confirmed, unaffected by worst\" }\n          - { model: \"Untrained readout\", R2: 0.686, worst_role: \"< Proj, training-dependent routing confirmed\" }\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Bar chart with error bars: 新增 CLIP-ViT bar 后，四方对比（SigLIP/CLIP/DINO/LLM），突出 R² 平坦 vs RSA 分化\"\n    analysis: >\n      Functional probe 在 worst 档下反而提供 silver lining：即使 Claim 1 被降级，\n      readout concentration（trained vs untrained）的 functional evidence 完全不受影响（p<0.0001），\n      是 routing-not-creating narrative 的最强量化支撑。\n\n  - name: \"CLIP-ViT pretraining control\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_012\"\n    description: \"用 CLIP ViT-L 替代 SigLIP，区分 VL pretraining 贡献 vs SigLIP-specific 效应\"\n    expected_results:\n      clip_vit_rsa_scenario_A: 0.39\n      clip_vit_rsa_scenario_B: 0.62\n      clip_vit_action_R2: 0.69\n      clip_vit_delta_R2: 0.09\n    result_rationale: >\n      这是 worst 档的 make-or-break 实验。两个 worst 场景：\n\n      场景 A（CLIP-ViT RSA ≈ 0.39，接近 DINO 0.388）：\n      CLIP ViT-L 的 contrastive pretraining（softmax cross-entropy, InfoNCE）与 DINO 的\n      self-supervised pretraining 产生类似的 geometric structure，RSA ≈ 0.39。\n      这直接说明 VL pretraining 不是 geometric alignment 的充分条件——CLIP 有 language supervision\n      但 geometric alignment 不比 DINO 好。SigLIP 的 RSA=0.615 来自其特定设计：\n      sigmoid loss 移除了 softmax 的 cross-sample normalization，允许更 fine-grained 的\n      per-pair alignment，可能产生与 action 空间更匹配的 geometric structure。\n      但这是 architecture/loss-specific 的 insight，不是 VL pretraining 的 general claim。\n      此时 R² ≈ 0.69（与 DINO 0.712 和 Projector 0.706 在同一水平），说明 action information\n      是 generic 的，所有 strong vision encoders 都有。\n\n      场景 B（CLIP-ViT RSA ≈ 0.62, > SigLIP 0.615）：\n      CLIP ViT-L 的 RSA 竟然更高，但 OpenVLA 选择了 SigLIP 且实际 downstream performance\n      更好。这意味着 RSA 与 VLA task performance 脱钩——高 geometric alignment 不等于好 VLA。\n      RSA 作为核心 metric 的 validity 被质疑。需要解释为什么 OpenVLA 团队选 SigLIP 而非 CLIP\n      （可能是 training efficiency / resolution / tokenizer 兼容性而非 representational 原因）。\n      此时论文必须转向方向 B：metric dissociation 本身是贡献，而非 RSA 的绝对值。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"CLIP-ViT Worst Scenario A: VL ≠ geometric alignment\"\n        rows:\n          - { model: \"SigLIP\", rsa: 0.615, R2: 0.706, interpretation: \"SigLIP-specific, not VL-general\" }\n          - { model: \"CLIP-ViT\", rsa: 0.39, R2: 0.69, interpretation: \"VL pretraining ≠ geometric alignment\" }\n          - { model: \"DINO\", rsa: 0.388, R2: 0.712, interpretation: \"≈ CLIP-ViT in both metrics\" }\n      - title: \"CLIP-ViT Worst Scenario B: RSA-performance dissociation\"\n        rows:\n          - { model: \"CLIP-ViT\", rsa: 0.62, R2: 0.69, interpretation: \"Highest RSA but not chosen for OpenVLA\" }\n          - { model: \"SigLIP\", rsa: 0.615, R2: 0.706, interpretation: \"Chosen for OpenVLA, slightly lower RSA\" }\n          - { model: \"DINO\", rsa: 0.388, R2: 0.712, interpretation: \"Lowest RSA, highest R²\" }\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Scenario A: RSA bar chart with CLIP-ViT ≈ DINO << SigLIP，标注 'VL pretraining ≠ sufficient'\"\n      - \"Scenario B: RSA vs downstream performance scatter，标注 dissociation\"\n    analysis: >\n      Plan_012 是 worst 档的定义性实验。无论场景 A 还是 B，Claim 1 都需要重写：\n      场景 A → \"SigLIP's sigmoid loss produces uniquely high geometric alignment, distinct from\n      both contrastive VL (CLIP) and self-supervised (DINO) pretraining\"。\n      场景 B → \"High geometric alignment (RSA) does not predict VLA backbone suitability;\n      metric selection critically shapes conclusions about representation quality\"。\n      两种场景下 Claim 2 和 Claim 3 不受影响——LLM degradation 和 routing-not-creating\n      不依赖 SigLIP 的 RSA 来源。Intro 和 framing 需要 ~2 天重写。\n      论文仍可投 CoRL 2026（接受 analysis/understanding 论文），但标题和 contribution statement\n      必须重构。\n\n  - name: \"Reviewer simulation (worst-tier consensus)\"\n    plan_id: \"n/a\"\n    description: \"模拟 worst 档下 reviewer 反应\"\n    expected_results:\n      reviewer_score_median: 4\n      reviewer_score_range: [3, 5]\n      consensus: \"scope narrow + metric dependency unresolved\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Worst 档下预期 reviewer 反应：\n      R1 (score 3): \"Single architecture (OpenVLA), single benchmark (LIBERO-Goal main results),\n      and the CLIP-ViT result undermines the core VL-pretraining claim. What remains is\n      observations specific to SigLIP in OpenVLA — not generalizable.\"\n      R2 (score 5): \"The routing-not-creating finding (Claim 3) is novel and well-supported\n      with strong statistics (p<0.0001). The metric dissociation (RSA vs CKA vs R²) is\n      a useful methodological contribution. Paper needs better framing but the evidence is solid.\"\n      R3 (score 4): \"Interesting analysis but the paper tries to do too much.\n      Pick either the routing story OR the metric dissociation story and do it thoroughly.\n      LIBERO-Spatial results (if included) weaken rather than strengthen the claims.\"\n      AC synthesis: Borderline. Strong evidence for Claim 3, but Claim 1 overreach and\n      metric dependency concern. Revision can fix if framing is tightened.\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Worst-tier Reviewer Score Distribution\"\n        rows:\n          - { reviewer: \"R1 (generalizability hawk)\", score: 3, main_concern: \"Single arch + CLIP-ViT undermines VL claim\" }\n          - { reviewer: \"R2 (methodology appreciator)\", score: 5, main_concern: \"Framing needs work but evidence is solid\" }\n          - { reviewer: \"R3 (scope clarity)\", score: 4, main_concern: \"Too many claims, pick one story\" }\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      Median score 4 = borderline reject/accept depending on AC disposition.\n      重构方向 A（routing-not-creating focus）更有可能获得 accept，因为证据集中且统计功效强。\n      方向 B（metric dissociation）风险更高——reviewer 可能认为是 negative result dressed up，\n      但如果执行得当（CKA-RSA-R² 三重分离作为方法论框架），也有 accept 路径。\n      关键：无论哪个方向，Claim 1 必须降级为 observation，否则 R1 的 score 会拖垮全文。\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":335,"cache_read_input_tokens":37581,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":335},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f38db59a-3a00-4c34-a2f2-7814e0d4d5d6","uuid":"060141af-f05c-4423-96ca-05b54af7f56c"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":189182,"duration_api_ms":190654,"num_turns":2,"result":"```yaml\ntier: worst\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  CLIP-ViT 打破 VL-pretraining 解释（RSA ≈ DINO 或 RSA > SigLIP），核心 framing 需重构。\n  放弃 \"vision encoder dominance\" 作为 general claim。\n  重构方向 A: \"Fine-Tuning Teaches Routing, Not Representation\"，聚焦 Claim 2+3，Claim 1 降级为 observation。\n  重构方向 B: \"Metric Dissociation\" framing，若 CLIP-ViT RSA > SigLIP 且 R² < SigLIP，\n  则 geometric-functional dissociation 本身成为核心贡献。\n  Claim 3 的 routing-not-creating 在任何场景下都成立，是 worst case 的保底叙事锚点。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  - name: \"SigLIP+Projector RSA vs Full VLA vs DINO\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_001\"\n    description: \"SigLIP+Projector RSA 对比 Full VLA 和 DINO，证明 action-relevant 结构源自 frozen vision encoder\"\n    expected_results:\n      siglip_projector_rsa: 0.615\n      trained_with_inst_rsa: 0.501\n      untrained_with_inst_rsa: 0.485\n      dino_rsa: 0.388\n    result_rationale: >\n      此实验已完成，数据不变。但在 worst 档下，这些结果的解释力被 plan_012 CLIP-ViT 结果削弱：\n      如果 CLIP-ViT RSA ≈ 0.39（≈ DINO），则 SigLIP 的高 RSA 不来自 \"VL pretraining\" 大类，\n      而来自 SigLIP 特定训练配方（sigmoid loss + batch design）。\n      SigLIP 0.615 的优势变成一个 architecture-specific observation 而非 generalizable claim。\n      如果 CLIP-ViT RSA > 0.60（> SigLIP），则 RSA 与下游性能脱钩（OpenVLA 用 SigLIP 而非 CLIP，\n      说明高 RSA 不等于好的 VLA backbone），RSA 作为核心 metric 的 validity 被质疑。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"RSA Comparison (unchanged, but reinterpreted)\"\n        rows:\n          - { model: \"SigLIP+Projector\", rsa: 0.615, worst_interpretation: \"SigLIP-specific, not VL-general\" }\n          - { model: \"VLA trained\", rsa: 0.501, worst_interpretation: \"LLM degradation holds regardless\" }\n          - { model: \"VLA untrained\", rsa: 0.485, worst_interpretation: \"Architecture-driven, training-invariant\" }\n          - { model: \"DINO\", rsa: 0.388, worst_interpretation: \"Vision-only baseline, may ≈ CLIP-ViT\" }\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Bar chart: SigLIP >> VLA >> DINO 仍成立，但新增 CLIP-ViT bar 后 narrative 需修改\"\n    analysis: >\n      数据本身不受影响。Worst 档的冲击来自 plan_012：CLIP-ViT 的位置决定 SigLIP 优势的归因。\n      Claim 1 必须从 \"VL pretraining produces geometric alignment\" 降级为\n      \"SigLIP provides highest geometric alignment in OpenVLA\"——一个 observation 而非 mechanism claim。\n\n  - name: \"DINO baseline RSA\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_002\"\n    description: \"Standalone vision model 参照基线\"\n    expected_results:\n      dino_rsa: 0.388\n      dino_action_R2: 0.712\n    result_rationale: >\n      已完成，数据不变。Worst 档下的关键重解读：DINO RSA=0.388 可能与 CLIP-ViT 接近（worst 预测\n      CLIP-ViT RSA ∈ [0.35, 0.42]）。这意味着 CLIP（VL-pretrained）和 DINO（self-supervised）\n      在 geometric alignment 上无显著差异，VL pretraining 不是 geometric alignment 的充分条件。\n      但 DINO 的 action R²=0.712 ≈ Projector 0.706 已说明 action information presence 与\n      geometric alignment 是不同维度——这个 dissociation 在 worst 档下反而更突出。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Scatter: RSA vs R² 二维图中，DINO 和 CLIP-ViT 聚集在低 RSA / 高 R² 区域，SigLIP 独占高 RSA / 高 R² 角\"\n    analysis: >\n      DINO 数据不变，但其角色从 \"vision-only 下界\" 变为 \"与 CLIP-ViT 共同构成 non-SigLIP cluster\"，\n      强化 metric dissociation narrative。\n\n  - name: \"Per-layer RSA degradation curve\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_003\"\n    description: \"追踪 RSA 从 projector output 到 LLM 各层的衰减轨迹\"\n    expected_results:\n      proj_rsa: 0.615\n      peak_llm_rsa: 0.488\n      proj_to_l1_drop_pct: \"20-40%\"\n      total_degradation: 0.13\n    result_rationale: >\n      已完成，数据不变。Worst 档下，per-layer curve 的解释力不受 CLIP-ViT 结果影响：\n      无论 SigLIP 的 geometric advantage 来自何处，LLM 对 geometric alignment 的降解是确定的\n      （0.615→0.488）。这条证据直接支持 Claim 2（LLM redistributes），与 Claim 1 的 scope 缩减无关。\n      在重构方向 A 下，per-layer curve 升级为核心 figure（从 supporting 变为 main evidence）。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Per-layer RSA worst-tier role\"\n        rows:\n          - { metric: \"Proj→L1 drop\", value: \"0.13-0.25\", role: \"Core evidence for Claim 2, unaffected by worst\" }\n          - { metric: \"Non-monotonic pattern\", value: \"yes\", role: \"Supports redistribution narrative\" }\n          - { metric: \"All LLM >> DINO\", value: \"yes\", role: \"Architecture matters even if VL-pretraining doesn't explain SigLIP\" }\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Per-layer RSA curve: 从 Claim 1 的 supporting figure 升级为 Claim 2 的 main figure\"\n    analysis: >\n      Worst 档下此实验的价值反而上升——当 Claim 1 被降级时，Claim 2 的 LLM degradation + redistribution\n      成为论文核心贡献之一，per-layer curve 是其关键可视化证据。\n\n  - name: \"Output head analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_004\"\n    description: \"确认 SigLIP+projector frozen，LLM 权重变化不传导到表征\"\n    expected_results:\n      vision_projector_cos_sim: 1.0\n      llm_rel_change_range: [1.22, 1.37]\n      head_vs_llm_ratio: 1.12\n    result_rationale: >\n      已完成，数据不变。Worst 档下，\"SigLIP+projector frozen\" 的意义发生微妙变化：\n      原 narrative 是 \"frozen vision encoder 提供 action structure，所以 Claim 1 成立\"。\n      Worst 档下变为 \"frozen SigLIP 提供最高 geometric alignment，但这可能是 SigLIP-specific\n      而非 VL-pretraining-general\"。Frozen 属性本身仍解释 trained ≈ untrained（Claim 3），\n      所以此实验对 routing-not-creating narrative 的支持不变。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      此实验在 worst 档下对 Claim 3 的支持力不变。对 Claim 1 的支持从 \"frozen encoder is the source\"\n      变为 \"frozen encoder explains training invariance\"，scope 缩窄但逻辑链不断。\n\n  - name: \"6 probing methods × 2 benchmarks\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_005\"\n    description: \"系统性验证 trained ≈ untrained\"\n    expected_results:\n      trained_vs_untrained_delta: \"≈0 across all methods\"\n      all_methods_consistent: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      Orphaned 但子实验已完成。数据支持 trained ≈ untrained。Worst 档下此结论不受威胁——\n      training invariance 是 Claim 3 的基础，与 CLIP-ViT 结果无关。即使 CLIP-ViT 打破 Claim 1，\n      routing-not-creating 的证据链（trained ≈ untrained in distributed representations,\n      trained >> untrained in readout concentration）完全独立。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      Worst case 的保底叙事锚点。6 methods consistency 在任何档位下都是 strong evidence。\n\n  - name: \"Instruction ablation\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_006\"\n    description: \"去掉 instruction text 测 RSA 变化\"\n    expected_results:\n      delta_with_vs_no_inst: 0.004\n      gate_judgment: \"FAIL — instruction 无影响\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      已完成，数据不变。Worst 档下 instruction invariance 仍成立且价值不变：\n      它直接支持 Claim 3 的 \"三重不变性\"（training + instruction presence + instruction content），\n      与 vision encoder identity 无关。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      Instruction ablation 在所有三档下结论一致，是 Claim 3 最稳健的子证据之一。\n\n  - name: \"2×2 matrix (training × instruction)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_007\"\n    description: \"四条件全收敛验证\"\n    expected_results:\n      four_cell_range: [0.480, 0.490]\n      bootstrap_ci_includes_0: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      已完成，数据不变。2×2 矩阵在 worst 档下仍是 Claim 3 的核心证据：\n      四个 cell 收敛在 0.48-0.49 band 内，bootstrap CI 包含 0。\n      这个结果不依赖 CLIP-ViT 的位置，因为它测量的是 VLA 内部 training/instruction 的效应，\n      而非跨 encoder 的比较。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"2×2 Matrix (unchanged)\"\n        rows:\n          - { condition: \"trained+inst\", rsa: 0.488, worst_role: \"Claim 3 core\" }\n          - { condition: \"trained-no_inst\", rsa: 0.489, worst_role: \"Claim 3 core\" }\n          - { condition: \"untrained+inst\", rsa: 0.485, worst_role: \"Claim 3 core\" }\n          - { condition: \"untrained-no_inst\", rsa: 0.480, worst_role: \"Claim 3 core\" }\n    figures_description:\n      - \"2×2 heatmap: 在 worst 档下从 supplementary 升级为 main text figure\"\n    analysis: >\n      Worst 档下，当 Claim 1 降级后，Claim 3 的 2×2 matrix 成为论文最 clean 的实验设计，\n      升级为 main figure 之一。\n\n  - name: \"Random instruction control\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_008\"\n    description: \"用随机/无意义 instruction 替代真实 instruction，验证 instruction content 不影响 RSA\"\n    expected_results:\n      normal_rsa: 0.489\n      random_rsa: 0.484\n      shuffled_rsa: 0.483\n      empty_rsa: 0.472\n      max_absolute_delta: 0.017\n    result_rationale: >\n      已完成，数据不变。四种 instruction 条件下 RSA 差异 < 0.02，完成三重不变性的第三重。\n      Worst 档下价值不变——instruction content invariance 是独立于 encoder identity 的发现。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      与 plan_006、plan_007 共同构成 Claim 3 不可撼动的证据基础。Worst 档不影响。\n\n  - name: \"CKA verification\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_009\"\n    description: \"用 CKA 指标重复 RSA 发现，确认或否认 metric dependency\"\n    expected_results:\n      cka_ordering: \"untrained > trained > projector > DINO (反转 RSA ordering)\"\n      cka_last_preaction: 0.127\n      rsa_cka_dissociation: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      已完成。RSA-CKA dissociation 在 worst 档下的角色发生质变：\n      原本是 \"需要讨论的 limitation\"（metric dependency），worst 档下变成核心贡献之一。\n      如果选择重构方向 B（Metric Dissociation framing），CKA-RSA-R² 三重分离\n      本身就是方法论贡献：RSA 捕捉 geometric alignment（SigLIP wins），CKA 捕捉 global structure\n      preservation（untrained wins），R² 捕捉 functional decodability（DINO ≈ SigLIP）。\n      三个 metric 三种排序 = 单一 metric 不足以评估 VLA 表征质量。\n      CLIP-ViT 如果 RSA > SigLIP 且 R² < SigLIP，则是第四个分离维度，进一步强化此论点。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Triple Metric Dissociation (worst-tier core contribution)\"\n        rows:\n          - { metric: \"RSA (geometric)\", ordering: \"SigLIP > trained > untrained > DINO\", captures: \"local distance structure alignment\" }\n          - { metric: \"CKA (global)\", ordering: \"untrained > trained > SigLIP > DINO\", captures: \"global structure preservation\" }\n          - { metric: \"R² (functional)\", ordering: \"readout > DINO ≈ SigLIP > LLM_img_mean\", captures: \"action decodability\" }\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Triple ordering reversal diagram: 三个 metric 的排序箭头交叉，每个 metric 讲不同故事\"\n    analysis: >\n      Worst 档下 plan_009 从 P2 实验升级为核心贡献。Metric dissociation 在 best/mid 档是\n      limitation discussion，在 worst 档是 main finding。方向 B 的论文标题可能变为\n      \"No Single Metric Captures VLA Representation Quality: A Multi-Metric Dissociation Analysis\"。\n\n  - name: \"LIBERO-Spatial cross-benchmark\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_010\"\n    description: \"第三个 benchmark 交叉验证所有 claims\"\n    expected_results:\n      libero_spatial_siglip_rsa: 0.42\n      libero_spatial_trained_rsa: 0.38\n      libero_spatial_untrained_rsa: 0.40\n      libero_spatial_dino_rsa: 0.35\n      libero_spatial_training_delta_p: 0.02\n      libero_spatial_readout_delta: 0.010\n      ordering_reversal: true\n      training_invariance_broken: \"possibly — p=0.02 < 0.05\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Worst 档核心预测：LIBERO-Spatial 的 action 空间结构与 LIBERO-Goal 不同（spatial reasoning\n      vs goal-directed manipulation），可能导致：\n      (1) SigLIP RSA 从 0.615 跌至 ~0.42——SigLIP 的 geometric alignment 在 spatial tasks\n      上远不如 goal tasks 突出，因为 SigLIP 的 VL pretraining 偏向 object-centric 而非 spatial。\n      (2) 排序反转：untrained RSA (0.40) > trained RSA (0.38)——random LLM 保留更多\n      spatial structure（因为 trained LLM 的 attention 被 LIBERO-Goal 的 fine-tuning 分布偏置，\n      对 out-of-distribution 的 spatial tasks 反而更差）。\n      (3) Training invariance 边缘打破：Δ=0.02, p≈0.02——CI 不包含 0 但效应小，\n      说明 training invariance 是 distribution-dependent 而非 architectural guarantee。\n      (4) Readout concentration delta 缩小到 0.010（vs LIBERO-Goal 的 0.045），\n      因为 routing 是 task-specific learned behavior，out-of-distribution 时效果衰减。\n      综合：LIBERO-Spatial 不支持 clean Claim 3 narrative，需要加 distribution-dependency caveat。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"LIBERO-Spatial vs LIBERO-Goal Comparison (worst-tier)\"\n        rows:\n          - { metric: \"SigLIP RSA\", libero_goal: 0.615, libero_spatial: 0.42, delta: -0.195, interpretation: \"Spatial tasks expose SigLIP weakness\" }\n          - { metric: \"Trained RSA\", libero_goal: 0.501, libero_spatial: 0.38, delta: -0.121, interpretation: \"Overall alignment drops\" }\n          - { metric: \"Untrained RSA\", libero_goal: 0.485, libero_spatial: 0.40, delta: -0.085, interpretation: \"Less degradation → ordering reversal\" }\n          - { metric: \"Training Δ p-value\", libero_goal: 0.20, libero_spatial: 0.02, delta: \"n/a\", interpretation: \"Invariance breaks at p<0.05\" }\n          - { metric: \"Readout Δ\", libero_goal: 0.045, libero_spatial: 0.010, delta: -0.035, interpretation: \"Routing is distribution-specific\" }\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Side-by-side per-layer curves: LIBERO-Goal (clean separation) vs LIBERO-Spatial (messy, overlapping bands)\"\n      - \"Bootstrap CI comparison: LIBERO-Goal CI includes 0, LIBERO-Spatial CI excludes 0\"\n    analysis: >\n      LIBERO-Spatial 在 worst 档下对 Claim 3 造成最严重威胁。Training invariance 的 p<0.05 break\n      意味着 \"routing-not-creating\" 不是 universal statement，而是 in-distribution observation。\n      论文需要加 distribution-dependency qualification：\"Training teaches distribution-specific routing;\n      distributed representations remain approximately invariant within the fine-tuning distribution.\"\n      这削弱了 Claim 3 的 generality 但不 falsify 它。\n      但如果 readout Δ 也缩小到 noise level（0.010, p>0.05），则 routing narrative 本身\n      受质疑——trained LLM 在 OOD 时既不 route 也不 create，只是 pass through。\n\n  - name: \"Functional action probe (three-way)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_011\"\n    description: \"Projector / LLM / DINO 三方 functional probe 对比\"\n    expected_results:\n      projector_R2: 0.706\n      llm_image_mean_R2: 0.683\n      llm_readout_R2: 0.731\n      dino_R2: 0.712\n      untrained_readout_R2: 0.686\n      bootstrap_proj_vs_llm_p: 0.001\n    result_rationale: >\n      Orphaned 但子实验已完成，数据不变。Worst 档下 functional probe 的关键重解读：\n      DINO R²=0.712 ≈ Projector R²=0.706 (p=0.22) 已经是 worst-direction 的证据——\n      action information presence 不区分 VL-pretrained 和 self-supervised encoder。\n      如果 CLIP-ViT R² 也 ≈ 0.70（与 DINO/SigLIP 同水平），则 \"所有 modern vision encoders\n      都包含足够的 action-relevant information\" 成为 finding，而非 SigLIP dominance。\n      如果 CLIP-ViT R² < 0.65（显著低于 DINO/SigLIP），则与 CLIP-ViT RSA > 0.60 形成\n      RSA-R² dissociation（高 geometric alignment 低 functional capacity），\n      是方向 B metric dissociation 的核心证据。\n      Readout concentration（trained 0.731 >> untrained 0.686, p<0.0001）不受 worst 档影响，\n      仍是 Claim 2+3 的最强 functional evidence。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Functional Probe under Worst Tier\"\n        rows:\n          - { model: \"SigLIP+Proj\", R2: 0.706, worst_role: \"≈ DINO, not special in R²\" }\n          - { model: \"DINO\", R2: 0.712, worst_role: \"≈ Proj, action info is generic\" }\n          - { model: \"LLM img_mean\", R2: 0.683, worst_role: \"Degradation confirmed, Claim 2 holds\" }\n          - { model: \"Trained readout\", R2: 0.731, worst_role: \"Routing confirmed, unaffected by worst\" }\n          - { model: \"Untrained readout\", R2: 0.686, worst_role: \"< Proj, training-dependent routing confirmed\" }\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Bar chart with error bars: 新增 CLIP-ViT bar 后，四方对比（SigLIP/CLIP/DINO/LLM），突出 R² 平坦 vs RSA 分化\"\n    analysis: >\n      Functional probe 在 worst 档下反而提供 silver lining：即使 Claim 1 被降级，\n      readout concentration（trained vs untrained）的 functional evidence 完全不受影响（p<0.0001），\n      是 routing-not-creating narrative 的最强量化支撑。\n\n  - name: \"CLIP-ViT pretraining control\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_012\"\n    description: \"用 CLIP ViT-L 替代 SigLIP，区分 VL pretraining 贡献 vs SigLIP-specific 效应\"\n    expected_results:\n      clip_vit_rsa_scenario_A: 0.39\n      clip_vit_rsa_scenario_B: 0.62\n      clip_vit_action_R2: 0.69\n      clip_vit_delta_R2: 0.09\n    result_rationale: >\n      这是 worst 档的 make-or-break 实验。两个 worst 场景：\n\n      场景 A（CLIP-ViT RSA ≈ 0.39，接近 DINO 0.388）：\n      CLIP ViT-L 的 contrastive pretraining（softmax cross-entropy, InfoNCE）与 DINO 的\n      self-supervised pretraining 产生类似的 geometric structure，RSA ≈ 0.39。\n      这直接说明 VL pretraining 不是 geometric alignment 的充分条件——CLIP 有 language supervision\n      但 geometric alignment 不比 DINO 好。SigLIP 的 RSA=0.615 来自其特定设计：\n      sigmoid loss 移除了 softmax 的 cross-sample normalization，允许更 fine-grained 的\n      per-pair alignment，可能产生与 action 空间更匹配的 geometric structure。\n      但这是 architecture/loss-specific 的 insight，不是 VL pretraining 的 general claim。\n      此时 R² ≈ 0.69（与 DINO 0.712 和 Projector 0.706 在同一水平），说明 action information\n      是 generic 的，所有 strong vision encoders 都有。\n\n      场景 B（CLIP-ViT RSA ≈ 0.62, > SigLIP 0.615）：\n      CLIP ViT-L 的 RSA 竟然更高，但 OpenVLA 选择了 SigLIP 且实际 downstream performance\n      更好。这意味着 RSA 与 VLA task performance 脱钩——高 geometric alignment 不等于好 VLA。\n      RSA 作为核心 metric 的 validity 被质疑。需要解释为什么 OpenVLA 团队选 SigLIP 而非 CLIP\n      （可能是 training efficiency / resolution / tokenizer 兼容性而非 representational 原因）。\n      此时论文必须转向方向 B：metric dissociation 本身是贡献，而非 RSA 的绝对值。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"CLIP-ViT Worst Scenario A: VL ≠ geometric alignment\"\n        rows:\n          - { model: \"SigLIP\", rsa: 0.615, R2: 0.706, interpretation: \"SigLIP-specific, not VL-general\" }\n          - { model: \"CLIP-ViT\", rsa: 0.39, R2: 0.69, interpretation: \"VL pretraining ≠ geometric alignment\" }\n          - { model: \"DINO\", rsa: 0.388, R2: 0.712, interpretation: \"≈ CLIP-ViT in both metrics\" }\n      - title: \"CLIP-ViT Worst Scenario B: RSA-performance dissociation\"\n        rows:\n          - { model: \"CLIP-ViT\", rsa: 0.62, R2: 0.69, interpretation: \"Highest RSA but not chosen for OpenVLA\" }\n          - { model: \"SigLIP\", rsa: 0.615, R2: 0.706, interpretation: \"Chosen for OpenVLA, slightly lower RSA\" }\n          - { model: \"DINO\", rsa: 0.388, R2: 0.712, interpretation: \"Lowest RSA, highest R²\" }\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Scenario A: RSA bar chart with CLIP-ViT ≈ DINO << SigLIP，标注 'VL pretraining ≠ sufficient'\"\n      - \"Scenario B: RSA vs downstream performance scatter，标注 dissociation\"\n    analysis: >\n      Plan_012 是 worst 档的定义性实验。无论场景 A 还是 B，Claim 1 都需要重写：\n      场景 A → \"SigLIP's sigmoid loss produces uniquely high geometric alignment, distinct from\n      both contrastive VL (CLIP) and self-supervised (DINO) pretraining\"。\n      场景 B → \"High geometric alignment (RSA) does not predict VLA backbone suitability;\n      metric selection critically shapes conclusions about representation quality\"。\n      两种场景下 Claim 2 和 Claim 3 不受影响——LLM degradation 和 routing-not-creating\n      不依赖 SigLIP 的 RSA 来源。Intro 和 framing 需要 ~2 天重写。\n      论文仍可投 CoRL 2026（接受 analysis/understanding 论文），但标题和 contribution statement\n      必须重构。\n\n  - name: \"Reviewer simulation (worst-tier consensus)\"\n    plan_id: \"n/a\"\n    description: \"模拟 worst 档下 reviewer 反应\"\n    expected_results:\n      reviewer_score_median: 4\n      reviewer_score_range: [3, 5]\n      consensus: \"scope narrow + metric dependency unresolved\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Worst 档下预期 reviewer 反应：\n      R1 (score 3): \"Single architecture (OpenVLA), single benchmark (LIBERO-Goal main results),\n      and the CLIP-ViT result undermines the core VL-pretraining claim. What remains is\n      observations specific to SigLIP in OpenVLA — not generalizable.\"\n      R2 (score 5): \"The routing-not-creating finding (Claim 3) is novel and well-supported\n      with strong statistics (p<0.0001). The metric dissociation (RSA vs CKA vs R²) is\n      a useful methodological contribution. Paper needs better framing but the evidence is solid.\"\n      R3 (score 4): \"Interesting analysis but the paper tries to do too much.\n      Pick either the routing story OR the metric dissociation story and do it thoroughly.\n      LIBERO-Spatial results (if included) weaken rather than strengthen the claims.\"\n      AC synthesis: Borderline. Strong evidence for Claim 3, but Claim 1 overreach and\n      metric dependency concern. Revision can fix if framing is tightened.\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Worst-tier Reviewer Score Distribution\"\n        rows:\n          - { reviewer: \"R1 (generalizability hawk)\", score: 3, main_concern: \"Single arch + CLIP-ViT undermines VL claim\" }\n          - { reviewer: \"R2 (methodology appreciator)\", score: 5, main_concern: \"Framing needs work but evidence is solid\" }\n          - { reviewer: \"R3 (scope clarity)\", score: 4, main_concern: \"Too many claims, pick one story\" }\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      Median score 4 = borderline reject/accept depending on AC disposition.\n      重构方向 A（routing-not-creating focus）更有可能获得 accept，因为证据集中且统计功效强。\n      方向 B（metric dissociation）风险更高——reviewer 可能认为是 negative result dressed up，\n      但如果执行得当（CKA-RSA-R² 三重分离作为方法论框架），也有 accept 路径。\n      关键：无论哪个方向，Claim 1 必须降级为 observation，否则 R1 的 score 会拖垮全文。\n```","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"f38db59a-3a00-4c34-a2f2-7814e0d4d5d6","total_cost_usd":0.43950175,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":26075,"cache_read_input_tokens":49422,"output_tokens":9240,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":26075,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":9078,"cache_read_input_tokens":37581,"cache_creation_input_tokens":335,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":335},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":20697,"outputTokens":22,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.020807,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":3,"outputTokens":9240,"cacheReadInputTokens":49422,"cacheCreationInputTokens":26075,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.41869475,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"3c88a432-0a5a-4233-94df-b4197f356587"}
